course: dictionary
lesson: 5174
title: Isolate: apart, alone or on its own
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word isolate means to set one thing apart from others. It has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is right. «To isolate a part means to practise one small bit on its own, then join it back to the bars around it.» The clues on its own and join it back show that isolate means to take one part away from the rest.
explain: Look for clues around the word. In a health lesson, isolate means keep someone apart so a germ does not spread. In a science test, it means separate one thing from a mixture so you can study it. In a maths sum, isolate x means get x on its own on one side of the equation.
explain: Isolated can also describe a feeling. If a child is left out at break, they may feel isolated. Ask yourself: is something being separated, or is someone being left out? The words around the word will tell you which.
fact: Isolate is a verb: isolate, isolates, isolated, isolating.
fact: «Isolate» means to keep a person or thing apart from others, or to separate one thing from a group.
fact: «Isolated» can mean lonely and left out, as in «an isolated village».
fact: In maths, to isolate x means to get x on its own on one side of an equation.
fact: Isolating someone on purpose to make them feel left out is a kind of bullying.
exercise: «To isolate a part means to practise one small bit on its own, then join it back to the bars around it.» What does isolate mean here? | To forget the music completely | To join everything together into one big piece | *To practise one small bit on its own | To play as loudly as you can
exercise: A scientist wants a fair test, so she isolates one variable. What does isolate mean? | Mixes everything together | Makes it bigger | Throws it away | *Separates one thing so it can be studied
exercise: Maths: «Isolate x in the equation.» What is the aim? | Add x to both sides | Write x in capital letters | Make x equal to zero for ever | *Get x on its own on one side
test: Ravi feels isolated after moving to a new village. What does isolated mean? | Happy to be busy | Excited about new games | *Lonely and left out | Covered in dust
test: Sick children must isolate at home. What does isolate mean here? | Cook dinner for the whole family | Play outside with friends | Sleep in a different bed every night | *Keep apart from others to stop germs spreading
exam: Which sentence uses isolate to mean keep apart to stop a disease spreading? | Jamie will isolate his favourite boots | *The family must isolate at home until the illness passes | The team will isolate the winning goal | The baker will isolate the sweet smell
